Alias of `async_insert_busy_timeout_max_ms`.\n\n**Introduced in:** v24.2\n\n**History**\n\n- **24.2** — introduced with the default value `200`. The minimum value of the asynchronous insert timeout in milliseconds; async_insert_busy_timeout_ms is aliased to async_insert_busy_timeout_max_ms
Alias of `promql_evaluation_time`.\n\n**Introduced in:** v25.8\n\n**History**\n\n- **25.9** — the default value remained `auto`. The setting was renamed. The previous name is `evaluation_time`.\n- **25.8** — introduced with the default value `auto`. New experimental setting. At the time the setting was named `evaluation_time`, which is now an alias of it.
1	1
Alias of `enable_lightweight_update`.\n\n**Introduced in:** v25.5\n\n**History**\n\n- **25.8** — the default value changed from `0` to `1`. Lightweight updates were moved to Beta. Added an alias for setting \'allow_experimental_lightweight_update\'.\n- **25.5** — introduced with the default value `0`. A new setting. At the time the setting was named `allow_experimental_lightweight_update`, which is now an alias of it.
Allows lightweight updates, which write only the updated values to patch parts instead of rewriting whole data parts as a mutation does.\n\nIf disabled, the `UPDATE` statement throws an exception, and `ALTER TABLE ... UPDATE` and lightweight `DELETE` do not use lightweight updates even if `alter_update_mode` or `lightweight_delete_mode` request them (with `lightweight_force` or `lightweight_update_force` they throw an exception).\n\n**Type:** `Bool`\n\n**Default:** `1`\n\n**Introduced in:** v25.5\n\n**History**\n\n- **25.8** — the default value changed from `0` to `1`. Lightweight updates were moved to Beta. Added an alias for setting \'allow_experimental_lightweight_update\'.\n- **25.5** — introduced with the default value `0`. A new setting. At the time the setting was named `allow_experimental_lightweight_update`, which is now an alias of it.
If settings `min_age_to_force_merge_seconds` and\n`min_age_to_force_merge_on_partition_only` should respect setting\n`max_bytes_to_merge_at_max_space_in_pool`.\n\nPossible values:\n- `true`\n- `false`\n\n**Type:** `Bool`\n\n**Default:** `1`\n\n**Introduced in:** v25.1\n\n**History**\n\n- **26.2** — the default value changed from `0` to `1`. Limit part sizes even with min_age_to_force_merge_seconds by default\n- **25.1** — introduced with the default value `0`. New setting
Only has an effect in ClickHouse Cloud. A setting for testing purposes, do not change it\n\n**Type:** `UInt64`\n\n**Default:** `0`\n\n**Introduced in:** v24.10\n\n**History**\n\n- **25.7** — the default value remained `0`. Rename of distributed_cache_read_alignment\n- **24.10** — introduced with the default value `0`. A setting for ClickHouse Cloud
